---
import TennibotMachine from "../../../assets/newdesignimages/TennibotMachine.png";
import '../../../../public/styles/global.css'
---

<div class="bg-[#191A16] py-16 px-4">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
      
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-white text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight">
          WHAT IS A PICKLEBALL<br/>
          MACHINE <span class="text-lime-400">AND WHY IT'S<br/>
          ESSENTIAL</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          A <span class="text-lime-400 font-semibold">pickleball machine</span> is an automated training device that 
          launches pickleballs at consistent speeds and trajectories. 
          Unlike traditional ball machines that offer basic functionality, 
          modern AI-powered machines like the Tennibot Partner provide 
          programmable drills and adaptive training scenarios.
        </p>
        
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          The key difference between traditional and advanced machines 
          lies in <span class="text-lime-400 font-semibold">intelligent customization</span>. While basic machines simply 
          shoot balls at set intervals, AI-enhanced machines can vary shot 
          patterns, simulate real game situations, and adapt to your skill 
          level.
        </p>
        
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Tennibot's accuracy and shot customization capabilities make it 
          possible to practice specific techniques repeatedly, build muscle 
          memory, and improve consistency - all without needing a 
          practice partner.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <div class="lg:pl-8">
         <img     
          src={TennibotMachine.src}
          alt="Tennibot Mobile App Interface"     
          fetchpriority="high"
          class="max-w-full h-auto"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>